# Zemen Game / arada.click -- this deployment's REAL, live ingress config,
# not an aspirational one. This is a genuinely different server from the
# original Arada Bingo / arada.fun deployment (see README.md's "Domain and
# Cloudflare Tunnel" section for that deployment's own, separate, host
# -level-cloudflared-plus-external-Traefik architecture, which this file
# does not describe and is not a replacement for).
#
# For THIS server, cloudflared runs as one of this repo's own Docker
# containers (deploy/docker-compose.prod.yml's `cloudflared` service),
# routing straight to each Compose service by its plain service name --
# no separate, untracked Traefik stack in the loop. This is a deliberate
# choice, not an oversight: the arada.fun deployment's real Traefik config
# lives entirely outside git on that host, and a 2026-09-14 incident (see
# DECISIONS.md) found four of its routers had silently disappeared with
# zero version-controlled copy to recover from. Routing this deployment
# entirely through this one committed file closes that exact gap for
# arada.click from day one.
#
# The hostname *pattern* below still mirrors arada.fun's real, live
# scheme (docs/PRODUCTION_DOMAIN_AND_CLOUDFLARE.md) rather than the
# never-implemented app./admin./pay./bot./sms. scheme this file used to
# describe: one apex hostname carries both the Mini App/gateway and the
# Telegram webhook (split by path, the same way arada.fun's Traefik does
# it with a PathPrefix rule -- cloudflared's own ingress rules support the
# same hostname+path combination directly, no Traefik needed to reproduce
# it), and payments/admin each answer on two hostnames apiece for the
# same underlying container (agent portal shares the payments container,
# finance shares the admin container -- see that doc's "Why payments/
# agent and admin/finance are the same containers, twice").
#
# Copy to deploy/cloudflared/config.yml (gitignored, like deploy/.env) and
# fill in the real tunnel id. One-time setup, on the arada.click server
# itself (README.md's "Domain and Cloudflare Tunnel" section has the full
# walkthrough):
#   1. Install the cloudflared CLI.
#   2. `cloudflared tunnel login` -- authorizes against the Cloudflare
#      account arada.click's DNS is managed under.
#   3. `cloudflared tunnel create zemen-game` -- creates the tunnel,
#      prints its id, and writes a credentials JSON file; copy that file
#      to deploy/cloudflared/tunnel-credentials.json (gitignored).
#   4. `cloudflared tunnel route dns zemen-game <hostname>`, once per
#      hostname below (arada.click, www.arada.click, payments.arada.click,
#      agent.arada.click, admin.arada.click, finance.arada.click,
#      sms.arada.click) -- this is what actually creates the DNS records;
#      arada.click is on Cloudflare DNS, so every one of these is just a
#      new record under the same zone, no extra domain purchase needed.
#   5. Replace <TUNNEL_ID> below with the id step 3 printed.
#
# Ingress rules are evaluated top to bottom; the first matching rule wins
# (hostname alone, or hostname+path together), and the final catch-all is
# required by cloudflared itself. Every `service:` value is a plain Docker
# Compose service name, reachable only from inside this stack's own
# network -- exactly how gateway/admin/payments/bot already reach
# postgres/redis today.

tunnel: <TUNNEL_ID>
credentials-file: /etc/cloudflared/tunnel-credentials.json

ingress:
  # Telegram's webhook (POST /webhook) -- checked before the catch-all
  # gateway rule below since both share the apex hostname. PUBLIC_BASE_URL
  # must be exactly https://arada.click for this to match what bot.py
  # registers with Telegram.
  - hostname: arada.click
    path: ^/webhook$
    service: http://bot:8003
  # Mini App static files, player REST API, and the game WebSocket --
  # everything else on the apex hostname.
  - hostname: arada.click
    service: http://gateway:8000
  - hostname: www.arada.click
    service: http://gateway:8000
  # Chapa's real server-to-server webhook (POST /webhooks/chapa) --
  # PAYMENTS_PUBLIC_BASE_URL must match this exact hostname.
  - hostname: payments.arada.click
    service: http://payments:8002
  # Payment Agent Portal -- same container as payments.arada.click, a
  # second hostname for the same service (see docs/AGENT_DASHBOARD_
  # GUIDE.md). AGENT_PORTAL_BASE_URL must match this exact hostname.
  - hostname: agent.arada.click
    service: http://payments:8002
  # Admin console -- IP-allowlisted at the application layer
  # (ADMIN_IP_ALLOWLIST) regardless of this subdomain being public; the
  # allowlist is the real boundary, not the hostname. Trusts Cloudflare's
  # own CF-Connecting-IP header at the edge, same as arada.fun.
  - hostname: admin.arada.click
    service: http://admin:8001
  # Finance role -- same container as admin.arada.click, a second
  # hostname for the same service ("finance" is an admin_users.role, not
  # a separate app).
  - hostname: finance.arada.click
    service: http://admin:8001
  # Enterprise SMS Control Plane -- a separate product/console, its own
  # admin login page at /console (same admin_users accounts as
  # admin.arada.click; see DECISIONS.md 2026-09-07).
  - hostname: sms.arada.click
    service: http://sms:8006
  - service: http_status:404
